"Go straight, then turn right," he said.
I walk straight along the main road.
I see a small turn.
I think this is the end of the road.
I turn right early.
I enter into a small street.
The street is full of shops.
There are clothing shops and spice shops there.
There are big sacks in front of a shop.
The sacks are full of cardamom and pepper.
I stand there for a moment.
I look at those spices.
Then I look around.
Many people walk past me.
I do not know this place.
I am lost in this crowd.
